---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Average Cost to Resurface a Pool in 2026 | GK Swimming Pools"
  description="Wondering what pool resurfacing costs in the San Fernando Valley or Santa Clarita? Here's a straight breakdown by material, size, and what affects the final price."
  canonical="https://www.gkswimmingpools.com/blog/pool-resurfacing-cost"
>

  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "BlogPosting",
    "headline": "What Is the Average Cost to Resurface a Standard Inground Pool?",
    "description": "Wondering what pool resurfacing costs in the San Fernando Valley or Santa Clarita? Here's a straight breakdown by material, size, and what affects the final price.",
    "datePublished": "2026-07-28",
    "author": {
      "@type": "LocalBusiness",
      "name": "GK Swimming Pools",
      "telephone": "(818) 804-8204"
    },
    "publisher": {
      "@type": "LocalBusiness",
      "name": "GK Swimming Pools",
      "url": "https://www.gkswimmingpools.com"
    },
    "image": "https://www.gkswimmingpools.com/images/blog/pool-resurfacing-pebble-finish-santa-clarita.webp",
    "mainEntityOfPage": {
      "@type": "WebPage",
      "@id": "https://www.gkswimmingpools.com/blog/pool-resurfacing-cost"
    }
  })} />

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="blog-hero">
    <div class="blog-hero__bg">
      <img
        src="/images/blog/pool-resurfacing-pebble-finish-santa-clarita.webp"
        alt="Close-up of a pool being resurfaced with fresh plaster in Santa Clarita"
        fetchpriority="high"
        decoding="async"
        width="1400"
        height="480"
      />
    </div>
    <div class="container blog-hero__inner">
      <span class="eyebrow">Pool Remodeling</span>
      <h1>What Is the Average Cost to<br>Resurface a Pool?</h1>
      <div class="blog-hero__meta">
        <span>GK Swimming Pools</span>
        <span class="blog-hero__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span>6 min read</span>
        <span class="blog-hero__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span>July 28, 2026</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ARTICLE -->
  <article class="blog-article section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="blog-article__body">

        <div class="blog-intro">
          <p>If your pool's surface is looking rough, stained, or chalky, you're probably wondering what pool resurfacing actually costs before you commit. It's one of the most common questions we get from homeowners across the San Fernando Valley and Santa Clarita, so here's a straightforward breakdown.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- AVERAGE COST -->
        <div class="blog-section">
          <span class="eyebrow">The Numbers</span>
          <h2>Average Pool Resurfacing Cost</h2>
          <p>For a standard inground pool, most homeowners in our service area pay between <strong>$4,500 and $9,000</strong> for a full resurface, depending on the material and the size of the pool. Larger pools, custom shapes, and higher-end finishes push that number up.</p>
          <p>Here's a rough breakdown by material:</p>

          <div class="cost-cards">
            <div class="cost-card">
              <div class="cost-card__label">Plaster (Marcite)</div>
              <div class="cost-card__range">$4,500 – $6,500</div>
              <p>The most common and affordable option, though it typically needs replastering every 7 to 10 years.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="cost-card cost-card--featured">
              <div class="cost-card__badge">Most Popular</div>
              <div class="cost-card__label">Pebble Finish</div>
              <div class="cost-card__range">$6,500 – $9,500</div>
              <p>More durable and textured, often lasting 15 to 20 years. A better long-term investment for most pools.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="cost-card">
              <div class="cost-card__label">Tile</div>
              <div class="cost-card__range">$8,000 and up</div>
              <p>Usually paired with a full remodel rather than a standalone resurface, which affects the overall cost.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <p class="blog-note">These numbers reflect general pool renovation pricing in the LA area and can shift based on your pool's condition, equipment access, and current material costs.</p>
        </div>

        <hr class="blog-divider" />

        <!-- WHAT AFFECTS COST -->
        <div class="blog-section">
          <span class="eyebrow">Cost Factors</span>
          <h2>What Affects the Cost of Pool Replastering</h2>
          <p>A few things move the price up or down on any pool resurface job:</p>

          <ul class="blog-factor-list">
            <li>
              <strong>Pool size and surface area</strong>
              <span>Bigger pools need more material and labor, plain and simple. A 600 sq ft pool costs meaningfully more than a 350 sq ft one.</span>
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Current condition</strong>
              <span>If there's existing damage, cracks, or old plaster that needs to be chipped out first, that adds labor time and cost before the new surface even goes on.</span>
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Material choice</strong>
              <span>Plaster is the budget option while pebble costs more upfront but lasts longer. which often makes it the better value over time when you factor in fewer replasters.</span>
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Add-ons</strong>
              <span>Many homeowners resurface at the same time as other work. new tile, updated coping, or LED lighting. Bundling projects can save money compared to doing them separately.</span>
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Access to the pool</strong>
              <span>If equipment has to be brought in through a narrow side yard or over landscaping, that adds to labor costs. Tight access is common in older SFV homes.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <hr class="blog-divider" />

        <!-- SIGNS YOU NEED IT -->
        <div class="blog-section">
          <span class="eyebrow">Know the Signs</span>
          <h2>Signs Your Pool Needs Resurfacing</h2>
          <p>You don't need to wait until the surface is visibly failing to start planning. Watch for these:</p>

          <div class="blog-tip">
            <div class="blog-tip__label">Common Warning Signs</div>
            <p>Rough or sandpaper-like texture on the plaster walls and floor. Visible stains that won't come out with normal cleaning or chemical treatment. Chalky white residue on your skin after swimming. Cracks or chipping around the pool's edges or steps.</p>
          </div>

          <p>If you're seeing any of these, it's worth getting an inspection before small issues turn into bigger, more expensive repairs. A crack that gets ignored long enough can become a leak.</p>
        </div>

        <hr class="blog-divider" />

        <!-- ALWAYS NECESSARY -->
        <div class="blog-section">
          <span class="eyebrow">Good to Know</span>
          <h2>Is a Full Resurface Always Necessary?</h2>
          <p>Not always. Sometimes an <a href="/services/pool-remodeling">acid wash</a> or a more thorough cleaning can extend the life of your existing surface. especially if the plaster is otherwise in good shape and just stained. A quick inspection can tell you whether you're looking at a resurface, a repair, or just a deep clean, and it's worth getting that answer before assuming the worst.</p>
          <p>That's exactly why we do free on-site assessments. It takes 20 minutes, and it gives you a real answer instead of a guess.</p>
        </div>

        <hr class="blog-divider" />

        <!-- GETTING A QUOTE -->
        <div class="blog-section">
          <span class="eyebrow">Next Steps</span>
          <h2>Getting an Accurate Quote</h2>
          <p>Cost guides are a helpful starting point, but every pool is different. The real number depends on your pool's exact size, current condition, and the finish you choose. If you're comparing <a href="/services/pool-remodeling">pool renovation companies in Santa Clarita or the San Fernando Valley</a>, make sure whoever you're talking to actually inspects the pool in person rather than quoting off a phone call alone.</p>
          <p>GK Swimming Pools has been doing this work as a family business for three generations. We'll walk your pool with you, explain what's actually going on with the surface, and give you a straightforward quote with no pressure.</p>
          <div class="blog-cta-inline">
            <a href="/remodel-quote" class="btn btn--primary">Get a Free Estimate</a>
            <a href="tel:8188048204" class="btn btn--outline">(818) 804-8204</a>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <!-- CTA BAND -->
  <div class="cta-band">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Ready to Resurface Your Pool?</h2>
      <p>GK Swimming Pools serves Santa Clarita and the San Fernando Valley. Free on-site assessment, no obligation.</p>
      <a href="/remodel-quote" class="btn btn--primary">Get My Free Estimate</a>
    </div>
  </div>

</Layout>

<style>
  /* HERO */
  .blog-hero {
    position: relative;
    height: 480px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .blog-hero__bg {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
  }
  .blog-hero__bg img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: center;
  }
  .blog-hero__inner {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 2;
    height: 100%;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: flex-end;
    padding-bottom: var(--space-12);
    background: linear-gradient(to top, rgba(6,47,97,0.88) 0%, rgba(6,47,97,0.3) 60%, transparent 100%);
  }
  .blog-hero__inner .eyebrow { color: var(--color-aqua); margin-bottom: var(--space-3); }
  .blog-hero__inner h1 {
    color: var(--color-white);
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, var(--text-4xl));
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }
  .blog-hero__meta {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    color: rgba(255,255,255,0.7);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    font-weight: 600;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .blog-hero__dot {
    width: 4px; height: 4px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--color-aqua);
  }

  /* BODY */
  .blog-article__body {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .blog-intro {
    background: var(--color-mist);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--color-aqua);
    padding: var(--space-6) var(--space-8);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
    border-radius: 0 var(--radius-sm) var(--radius-sm) 0;
  }
  .blog-intro p {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    color: var(--color-deep);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .blog-section { margin-bottom: var(--space-12); }
  .blog-section .eyebrow { margin-bottom: var(--space-3); }
  .blog-section h2 { margin-bottom: var(--space-6); }
  .blog-section p { color: var(--color-muted); line-height: 1.85; margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
  .blog-section strong { color: var(--color-deep); }
  .blog-section a { color: var(--color-deep); font-weight: 700; text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }

  /* Cost cards */
  .cost-cards {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-4);
    margin: var(--space-6) 0;
  }
  .cost-card {
    background: var(--color-white);
    border: 1.5px solid var(--color-border);
    border-top: 3px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    padding: var(--space-6);
    position: relative;
  }
  .cost-card--featured {
    border-top-color: var(--color-aqua);
    box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(8,65,132,0.08);
  }
  .cost-card__badge {
    position: absolute;
    top: -1px;
    right: var(--space-4);
    background: var(--color-aqua);
    color: var(--color-deep);
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: 0.2rem 0.6rem;
    border-radius: 0 0 3px 3px;
  }
  .cost-card__label {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-deep);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }
  .cost-card__range {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-weight: 800;
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    color: var(--color-deep);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }
  .cost-card p {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .blog-note {
    font-size: var(--text-sm) !important;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-style: italic;
    background: var(--color-mist);
    padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-6);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
  }

  /* Factor list */
  .blog-factor-list {
    list-style: none;
    margin: var(--space-6) 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0;
  }
  .blog-factor-list li {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-1);
    padding: var(--space-5) 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    padding-left: var(--space-6);
    position: relative;
  }
  .blog-factor-list li::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: var(--space-6);
    width: 8px;
    height: 8px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--color-aqua);
  }
  .blog-factor-list strong {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    color: var(--color-deep);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
  }
  .blog-factor-list span {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-muted);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  /* Tip box */
  .blog-tip {
    background: var(--color-deep);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    padding: var(--space-6) var(--space-8);
    margin: var(--space-6) 0;
  }
  .blog-tip__label {
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-aqua);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }
  .blog-tip p {
    color: rgba(255,255,255,0.88);
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 100%;
  }

  .blog-divider {
    border: none;
    border-top: 2px solid var(--color-border);
    margin: var(--space-12) 0;
  }

  /* Inline CTA */
  .blog-cta-inline {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .blog-hero { height: 360px; }
    .cost-cards { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .blog-intro { padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-5); }
    .blog-cta-inline { flex-direction: column; }
  }
</style>
